---
title: Parippu Curry (Kerala dal with coconut)
country: India
region: Kerala (Kochi)
credit: Home cooks of Kochi, Kerala; taught in-game by Ammachi Leela
cook: ammachi-leela
difficulty: 1
skills: [legumes, heat-control, tempering]
servings: 3
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
status: draft
---
-- Draft until reviewed by a cook from this tradition.
Rinse @split moong dal{100%g} in a #bowl{} two or three times, until the water runs mostly clear.

Put the dal in a #pot{} with @water{500%ml}, @turmeric{1/4%tsp} and @green chillies{2}, slit lengthways. Simmer, part-covered, until soft enough to crush against the side with a spoon. Add a splash more water if it gets thick. ~{20%minutes}

While it cooks, grind @grated coconut{60%g} with @cumin seeds{1/2%tsp}, @garlic{1%clove} and a splash of water in a #blender{} to a smooth, thick paste.

Mash the dal lightly with the back of a #ladle{}. Stir in the coconut paste and @salt{3/4%tsp}. Bring back to a gentle bubble — no hard boil now, or the coconut splits — and simmer. ~{5%minutes}

For the tempering, heat @coconut oil{1%tbsp} in a #small pan{} over medium heat. Add @mustard seeds{1/2%tsp} and wait until they pop. ~{30%seconds}

Add @shallots{3}, thinly sliced, and @dried red chillies{2}. Fry until the shallots turn golden. ~{3%minutes}

Add @curry leaves{1%sprig} — stand back, they spit — stir for a few seconds, then pour the sizzling tempering over the dal. Serve with hot rice, a spoon of @ghee{1%tsp} if you like, and @pappadam{3}.
